## Frequently asked questions


### Can Postman do load testing?


Yes. Use the Collection Runner Performance mode to run virtual users concurrently. A functional collection run with repeated iterations is a different test.


### Can Postman run a load test in the cloud?


Postman supports cloud performance runs on eligible paid plans. This tutorial uses the desktop App runner because its target is a localhost API.


### Are virtual users the same as requests per second?


No. Virtual users repeat a request workflow. Its length and response times affect the throughput the test produces.


### Can I use proxymock with a Postman load test?


Yes. Postman can send inbound HTTP requests while proxymock supplies recorded responses for downstream dependencies. Configure unmatched-request behavior for the isolation the test needs.
